\description{
Registered rosters of both sides with player bio fields (the season registration, not the game box).

Endpoint: \verb{GET https://data-server.cbaleague.com/api/schedules/getPlayersByScheduleId/\{schedule_id\}}
}
\details{
\itemize{
\item Unofficial and unsupported: these wrappers read the routes that cbaleague.com's own data site (a Vue
single-page app) calls. SportsDataverse has not ruled on the site's terms, so payloads are not redistributed as
release assets. Requests are spaced at least 1 s apart per host; keep use small.
\item Access: every response body is AES-128-ECB encrypted with a public key shipped in the site's front-end bundle;
the runtime decrypts it with \code{digest::AES()} and refuses anything that does not decrypt. The host blocks
datacenter IPs at TCP: set the environment variable \code{CBA_PROXY} (or \code{options(hoopR.proxy = ...)}) to a
residential proxy URL; it is never printed or put in a condition. Without a proxy the request goes direct and,
from a datacenter, fails within seconds (a 5 s connect timeout, no retry of a refused or timed-out connect).
Where direct access works (a residential IP), set \code{CBA_DIRECT=1} for the full 60 s timeout and retries.
\item Seasons: the API's season is the START year; every \code{season} argument here is the END year (2026 = 2025-26) and
is sent as \code{season - 1}. Columns named \code{season} keep the wire value (the START year, so the sdv END year is
\code{season + 1}). The season list reaches 1995-96; box data before 2009-10 is unverified.
\item Coverage: game wrappers serve FINISHED games only. Each first reads the game report header (cached per
session), and an unfinished game raises \code{hoopR_asset_fetch}. Box, period, roster and best-player bodies are
checked against that header (points sum to the score, team ids match, advanced rows are box players).
Play-by-play is served one period per request: every period is fetched, and a partial set, an unordered clock
or a final score the plays do not reach is refused. Play-by-play is verified on 2017-18 and 2025-26 only and is
absent for 2009-10 (\code{hoopR_no_data}). There are NO shot x/y coordinates in this API (shot location exists only
as team and player zone splits), and play-by-play has no player or team ids (Chinese sentence text plus
surnames). Box data has 12-minute quarters in 2009-10 and 2017-18 and 10-minute quarters in 2025-26. The
women's CBA is not covered (no official source).
\item Not game data: \code{cba_game_team_shots()} and \code{cba_game_team_four()} answer the two teams' SEASON tables (the shot
zones are the teams' current profile; the four factors are the previous season), whichever game is asked for.
The reference lists (\code{cba_team_options()}, \code{cba_team_counts()}) and \code{cba_report_status()} are not echoed by the
API, so their scope is unchecked.
\item Duplicate rows: in some games (2025-26 game 100105799) the advanced-box and extras routes repeat player rows
(26 rows for 12 players), and the repeats are not always copies. \code{cba_player_advanced()} and
\code{cba_player_extras()} keep the FIRST row per \code{player_id}.
\item Text fields are Chinese (names, play-by-play sentences, position and nationality labels). The column
descriptions here are ASCII; sdv-py's \code{tools/codegen/notes/cba_glossary.yaml} holds the full English
glossaries.
\item Personal data: the operator ids (\code{createdBy} / \code{lastModifiedBy}, one holds a mobile number) and any bare
mobile-number string are removed from every body. Players' public bio fields (birth date, height, weight) are
kept.
\item Ids: \code{schedule_id} (games, one global 9-digit sequence 100xxxxxx), \code{team_id} (clubs, stable across sponsor
renames), \code{player_id} (persons) and \code{match_type_id} are integers. The roster registration \code{id} of
\code{cba_rosters()} is a 19-digit integer that an R integer or double cannot hold exactly, so it is kept as its
exact digits (character).
\item Errors are classed conditions: \code{hoopR_no_data} (HTTP 404, a game without play-by-play), \code{hoopR_bad_request} (a
non-integer id or season, HTTP 400 / 422) and \code{hoopR_asset_fetch} (any other non-200, including HTTP 500, which
this API answers for a body it dislikes and which is not retried; a dead connection; an empty or undecryptable
body; an unfinished game; a body for another game, team, season or day), all inheriting \code{hoopR_error}. HTTP 429
/ 502 / 503 / 504 are retried, up to three attempts. Wrappers raise; they never warn and return empty.
}
}
